   "source": "# Structs (and Concurrency)\n\n> Verified against crush-ast `aa07413` (2026-10-16).\n\nA struct is declared once (on one line), built with a literal, and given methods\nin an `impl` block. Structs are passed by reference.\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "done"
   },
   "meta": {},
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "examples-concurrency-structs-1",
   "kind": {
    "type": "crush"
   },
   "source": "struct Point { x: Float, y: Float }\nimpl Point {\n    fn new(x, y) { return Point { x: x, y: y } }\n    fn dist2(self, other) {\n        let dx = self.x - other.x\n        let dy = self.y - other.y\n        return dx * dx + dy * dy\n    }\n    fn label(self) { return \"(\" + self.x + \", \" + self.y + \")\" }\n}\n\nlet p = Point::new(1.0, 2.0)\nlet q = Point { x: 4.0, y: 6.0 }\n\nprint(\"p = \" + p.label())\nprint(\"squared distance: \" + p.dist2(q))\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "pending"
   },
   "meta": {
    "tags": [
     "guide",
     "runnable"
    ],
    "extra": {
     "guide": {
      "src": "examples/concurrency-structs.md:8",
      "browser": "run",
      "expect_output": "p = (1.0, 2.0)\nsquared distance: 25.0\n"
     }
    }
   },
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "examples-concurrency-structs-md-3",
   "kind": {
    "type": "markdown"
   },
   "source": "**What this shows:**\n\n- `struct Point { x: Float, y: Float }`: declare it on **one line**; the parser\n  does not yet accept a struct body that spans lines\n- `Point { x: 4.0, y: 6.0 }` names every field; `Point::new(...)` is a method\n  without `self`, called through the type\n- `p.dist2(q)` resolves `dist2` on `p`'s struct; `self` is `p`\n- `Float` arithmetic: `3.0 * 3.0 + 4.0 * 4.0` is `25.0`\n\nMore in [Structs, Methods and Kinds](https://docs.crushlang.org/crush/structs.html).\n\n## Concurrency\n\n`spawn` starts a green task; tasks take turns at `yield`, and `await` collects a\ntask's result. The workers below share one captured counter:\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "done"
   },
   "meta": {},
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "examples-concurrency-structs-2",
   "kind": {
    "type": "crush"
   },
   "source": "fn main() {\n    let done = 0\n    let worker = |name| {\n        print(name + \" running\")\n        yield\n        print(name + \" finishing\")\n        done = done + 1\n        return name\n    }\n    let a = spawn worker(\"a\")\n    let b = spawn worker(\"b\")\n    print(\"main\")\n    print(await a)\n    print(await b)\n    print(\"finished: \" + done)\n}\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "pending"
   },
   "meta": {
    "tags": [
     "guide",
     "runnable"
    ],
    "extra": {
     "guide": {
